+<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/MCT> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasLithology> "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/L"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI> .
+<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/MCT> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasLithology> "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/V"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI> .
+<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/MCT> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasLithologyDescription> "Clay-bound gravel or gravelly clay with flint and quartzite cobbles. Typically pale yellow-brown and orange mottled."@en .
+<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/MCT> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasLowerBoundaryDefinition> "Unconformably overlies bedrock (including Buchan Gravels Formation) and earlier East Grampian Glacigenic Subgroup till."@en .
+<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/MCT> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasThicknessDescription> "< 1 m to 3 m."@en .
+<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/MCT> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasUpperBoundaryDefinition> "Heavily weathered. In places overlain by peat and alluvium."@en .
+<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/MCT> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Clay, cobbles and gravel. Stratified superficial deposits. Occurs onshore. Formed during the Devensian Stage (Quaternary Period) (.116-.0118 Ma BP)."@en .
